{number: 149}
{title: Jesus Calls Us}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus calls us; o'er the [F] tumult
Of our [C] life's wild, restless [G7] sea,
[C] Day by day His sweet voice [F] soundeth,
Saying, [C] "Christian, [G7] follow [C] Me.“
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Jesus calls us from the [F] worship
Of the [C] vain world's golden [G7] store;
[C] From each idol that would [F] keep us,
Saying, [C] "Christian, [G7] love Me [C] more."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
In [C] our joys and in our [F] sorrows,
Days of [C] toil and hours of [G7] ease,
Still [C] He calls, in cares and [F] pleasures,
"That we [C] love Him [G7] more than [C] these.“
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Jesus calls us: by Thy [F] mercies,
Saviour, [C] may we hear Thy [G7] call,
Give [C] our hearts to Thine o-[F] bedience,
Serve and [C] love Thee [G7] best of [C] all.
{end_of_verse}
